  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social projects of the Colombian Jesuits</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to assist CINEP and the Colombian Jesuits. The overall aim of the Colombian Jesuits, of &#x2018;serving the faith and promoting justice,&#x2019; has been translated in Colombia into four specific dimensions: sustainable rural development, research and popular education, the creation of a peace culture, and support for displaced people.   

CAFOD funds CINEP, an institution that provides critical analysis through its research to offer an alternative model of development for Colombia. Its Peace Programme works to promote public participation and citizenship, and advocates a reduction in inequality and a state that serves the interests of its citizens. 

CAFOD&apos;s grants are for core support to CINEP and the Peace programme, with an element to support the Jesuits&apos; efforts to increase the integration between their social programmes. CINEP&#x2019;s 3-year plan, 2015-2017, represents a further stage in adjusting CINEP&#x2019;s work to the more focused and coordinated approach of the Colombian Jesuit province.</narrative>
  </description>
